---
description: "Cursor rules for checking that the app and its critical user journeys still work in a real browser after AI code changes, with stillworks."
globs: **/*
alwaysApply: true
---
When you change application code (not only docs, comments or tests), check the app still works before you say you're done:

1. Make sure the dev server is running.
2. If the project has `journeys.config.ts`, run `npx stillworks run --no-promo`. It runs signup, login, checkout and the other journeys in a real browser.
   If it doesn't, run `npx stillworks check http://localhost:3000 --no-promo` (use the dev server's URL). It opens the app and its key pages, read-only, and reports pages that don't load, "not found" screens, JavaScript crashes and failing API calls.
3. If it fails, read `verify-report/REPORT.md` and the screenshot it points to. Fix the root cause, starting from the failed requests and console errors.
   - Don't change files unrelated to the failure.
   - Don't edit `journeys.config.ts` to make a check pass.
4. Run it again until everything passes (at most 3 tries), then say what broke and what you changed.

Setup: `npx stillworks install` once for the browser. To write journeys: `npx stillworks init` (https://github.com/valmirjunior2109-spec/stillworks).
